sentials","k":"post_office","la":-33.044789,"lo":-71.621492,"d":968,"w":"https://www.chilexpress.cl/"},{"n":"Lavacentro Service","g":"essentials","k":"laundry","la":-33.045183,"lo":-71.621831,"d":984,"h":"Mo-Fr 09:30-13:30, 16:00-20:00; Sa 10:00-14:00","ph":"322230599"},{"n":"Bank of Chile","g":"essentials","k":"bank","la":-33.045749,"lo":-71.621967,"d":1028},{"n":"Iglesia de la Matriz","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":-33.0363,"lo":-71.6322,"d":434,"ds":"The Iglesia de La Matriz del Salvador (The Matriz Church of the Saviour) is a church in the city of Valparaíso, Chile. Located in the heart of the port district (Barrio Puerto) of the city, surrounded by cobblestone streets and houses, it has a historical importance in the city and was declared a National Monument of Chile in 1971.","wpu":"Iglesia de la Matriz","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e0/Iglesiadelamatriz_001.jpg/960px-Iglesiadelamatriz_001.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Aníbal Pinto Square","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":-33.043153,"lo":-71.624633,"d":653,"ds":"The Aníbal Pinto Square (Spanish: Plaza Aníbal Pinto) is a town square built on reclaimed land in Valparaíso, Chile. Formerly \"Plaza del Orden\" (Order Square), the Aníbal Pinto Square is named after President Aníbal Pinto. It features a fountain called \"Fuente de Neptuno\" (Fountain of Neptune), which was erected in 1892.","wpu":"Aníbal Pinto Square","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6e/Plaza_An%C3%ADbal_Pinto.jpg/960px-Plaza_An%C3%ADbal_Pinto.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Dissidents Cemetery","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":-33.045261,"lo":-71.625039,"d":853,"ds":"The Cemetery of Dissidents is on the Panteón hill, in front of the Cemetery nº 1 and at one side of the old city jail (now a cultural center) in Valparaíso, Chile. It was created in 1825 to hold the remains of the British and other Europeans residents, whose Protestant faith differed from the official state religion at the time, Roman Catholicism.","wpu":"Dissidents Cemetery","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/19/Cementerio_Ingl%C3%A9s_de_Valpara%C3%ADso-Entrada_Principal.JPG/960px-Cementerio_Ingl%C3%A9s_de_Valpara%C3%ADso-Entrada_Principal.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"British Arch","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":-33.04464,"lo":-71.62046,"d":1019,"ds":"The British Arch (Spanish: Arco Británico) is a monument on Brazil Avenue in Valparaíso, Chile. It was donated to the town in 1910 by the British community there to mark the centenary of the Independence of Chile. Designed by the Chilean architect Alfredo Azancot, the arch was unveiled in 1911.","wpu":"British Arch","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/79/Arco_Brit%C3%A1nico.jpg/960px-Arco_Brit%C3%A1nico.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Santiago Severín Library","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":-33.045,"lo":-71.619444,"d":1114,"ds":"Santiago Severín Library (Spanish: Biblioteca Santiago Severín) is a public library located in Valparaíso, Chile. It was the first public library created with the consent of the Chilean government and was established on 27 February 1873. It holds 80,000 volumes.","wpu":"Santiago Severín Library","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b2/Biblioteca_Santiago_Sever%C3%ADn.jpg/960px-Biblioteca_Santiago_Sever%C3%ADn.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"St. James Cathedral, Valparaíso","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":-33.0462,"lo":-71.619,"d":1239,"ds":"The Cathedral of St. James (Spanish: Catedral de Santiago en Valparaíso), in Valparaíso, Chile, is the cathedral of the Roman Catholic Diocese of Valparaíso in Chile. Also known simply as Valparaíso Cathedral, the cathedral church is located in the neighborhood of El Almendral neighborhood, on the east side of the Plaza de la Victoria.","wpu":"St. James Cathedral, Valparaíso","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f9/Catedral_de_Valpara%C3%ADso.jpg/960px-Catedral_de_Valpara%C3%ADso.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Sacred Hearts Church (Valparaíso)","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":-33.0484,"lo":-71.6155,"d":1641,"ds":"The Sacred Hearts Church (Spanish: Iglesia de los Sagrados Corazones) is a Catholic church located at 2086 Independencia Street, in El Almendral neighborhood, in Valparaíso, Chile. Staffed by the Congregation of the Sacred Hearts of Jesus and Mary, it was built to serve as the church for the Sacred Hearts School of Valparaíso community.","wpu":"Sacred Hearts Church (Valparaíso)","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/61/WLM_1839_fstar_view_01.JPG/960px-WLM_1839_fstar_view_01.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Capilla del Carmen (Valparaíso)","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":-33.0518,"lo":-71.6113,"d":2185,"ds":"The Capilla del Carmen, also known as Capilla de la Medalla Milagrosa, is a chapel located on the lower flank of El Litre Hill, in El Almendral neighborhood of Valparaíso, Chile. Built in 1928, it was run by the Daughters of Charity of Saint Vincent de Paul, who provided care to patients of the adjacent Hospital Carlos Van Buren until March 2017.","wpu":"Capilla del Carmen (Valparaíso)","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3c/CAPILLA_DEL_CARMEN_VALPARAISI.JPG/960px-CAPILLA_DEL_CARMEN_VALPARAISI.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Barón funicular","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":-33.04319,"lo":-71.60412,"d":2299,"ds":"The Barón funicular (Spanish: Ascensor Barón), built in 1906, is a funicular located on its namesake hill in Valparaíso, Chile, and was declared a Historic Monument on 1 September 1998.","wpu":"Barón funicular","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/ff/Ascensorbaron.JPG/960px-Ascensorbaron.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"San Francisco Church (Valparaíso)","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":-33.039494,"lo":-71.600481,"d":2570,"ds":"San Francisco Church (Spanish: Iglesia de San Francisco) is a Catholic church located in Barón Hill, Valparaíso, Chile. The church served as lighthouse to the navigants who were arriving Valparaíso until the early 20th century, being the first recognizable point of the city. Valparaíso is often nicknamed with the diminutive form of Francisco: Pancho.","wpu":"San Francisco Church (Valparaíso)","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/90/Iglesia_de_San_Francisco%2C_Cerro_Bar%C3%B3n%2C_Valpara%C3%ADso_20240817_01.jpg/960px-Iglesia_de_San_Francisco%2C_Cerro_Bar%C3%B3n%2C_Valpara%C3%ADso_20240817_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Wulff Castle","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":-33.01915,"lo":-71.565167,"d":6221,"ds":"Wulff Castle (Spanish: Castillo Wulff) is a historic castle overlooking the sea in Viña del Mar, Chile. It was built in 1906 for the Wulff family. It is the headquarters of the city heritage center.","wpu":"Wulff Castle","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4b/Castillo_Wulff1.JPG/960px-Castillo_Wulff1.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Palace of Cerro Castillo","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":-33.02,"lo":-71.5643,"d":6266,"ds":"The Palace of Cerro Castillo (Spanish: Palacio de Cerro Castillo) is the official country retreat and summer residence of the President of Chile. Built in 1929 in the Spanish Colonial Revival style, it is situated atop Cerro Castillo hill located in Viña del Mar and has been designated as a national and municipal historic monument.","wpu":"Palace of Cerro Castillo","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d4/Palacio_Presidencial_de_Cerro_Castillo.jpg/960px-Palacio_Presidencial_de_Cerro_Castillo.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},{"n":"Brunet Castle","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":-33.02178,"lo":-71.56206,"d":6406,"ds":"The Brunet Castle (Spanish: Castillo Brunet), also known as Yarur Palace (Spanish: Palacio Yarur), is a historic castle in Viña del Mar, Chile.","wpu":"Brunet Castle","img":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/6/68/Castillo_Brunet.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled"},{"n":"Quinta Vergara Amphitheater","g":"sights","k":"landmark","la":-33.029651,"lo":-71.552431,"d":7105,"ds":"The Quinta Vergara Amphitheater is an open-air theatre and concert venue within the Parque Quinta Vergara in Viña del Mar, Chile. It hosts the Viña del Mar International Song Festival held yearly in February. The venue is owned by the Viña del Mar Municipality.","wpu":"Quinta Vergara Amphitheater","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5c/Quinta_Vergara_2007.JPG/960px-Quinta_Vergara_2007.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"}],"about":{"ds":"Valparaíso is a major city, commune, seaport, and naval base facility in the Valparaíso Region of Chile. Valparaíso was originally named after Valparaíso de Arriba, in Castile-La Mancha, Spain. With a population of 284,938, it is the 10th-largest commune in Chile.","wpu":"Valparaíso","img":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/dd/Historic_Quarter_of_the_Seaport_City_of_Valpara%C3%ADso_04.jpg/960px-Historic_Quarter_of_the_Seaport_City_of_Valpara%C3%ADso_04.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail"},"wk":"2026-10-18"}